<div id="@_d.I.ClassName" style="display: contents">
    <main id="main"><section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap page-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow"><a href="/jbhl">HOME</a> / HOME LOAN OPTIONS</p><h1>Understand what borrowing against your property involves.</h1><p class="hero-lead">A second mortgage may provide a way to access funds while keeping an existing home loan in place. We will help you weigh the costs and risks.</p><a class="button button-lime" href="/jbhl/contact">Discuss a second mortgage <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="page-hero-image" role="img" aria-label="Australian home in a landscaped garden"></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap content-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHAT TO CONSIDER</p><h2>Second mortgages: start with your situation.</h2><p>There is no single loan structure that suits everyone. We will talk through what you want to achieve, how a loan could fit your budget and what you should understand before applying.</p></div><div class="detail-rows"><div class="detail-row"><span>01</span><div><h3>Understand the need</h3><p>We start with the amount you need, its purpose and whether another lending structure may suit you.</p></div></div><div class="detail-row"><span>02</span><div><h3>Review your property and loans</h3><p>Available equity, existing lending and your ability to repay all matter to an assessment.</p></div></div><div class="detail-row"><span>03</span><div><h3>Consider the consequences</h3><p>A second mortgage is secured by property. Missed repayments can put the property at risk, so costs and alternatives deserve careful attention.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="faq-section section"><div class="wrap faq-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">COMMON QUESTIONS</p><h2>A few things worth knowing.</h2></div><div class="faqs"><details><summary>What is a second mortgage?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>It is an additional loan secured against a property that already has a mortgage. It is separate from your existing loan, with its own terms and costs.</p></details><details><summary>Is it the same as refinancing?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. Refinancing generally replaces an existing loan; a second mortgage adds another secured loan. Which option is suitable depends on your circumstances.</p></details></div></div></section><section class="cta-band"><div class="wrap cta-inner"><div><p class="eyebrow">A conversation can be a good start</p><h2>Let’s talk about your next step</h2><p>Tell us what you are hoping to do. Our team can help you understand the next step.</p></div><div class="cta-actions"><a class="button button-lime" href="/jbhl/contact">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="tel:1300795775" class="text-link light">Or call 1300 795 775</a></div></div></section></main>
</div>
